		"labeled detail bullets":               "## High\n\n### 1. Unbounded retry\n- **File:** retry.go:42\n- **Issue:** the loop never stops on 503.\n- **Fix:** cap attempts at 5.\n\n## Medium\n\nNone.",
		"labeled detail paragraphs":            "### High\n\n**Unbounded retry** (retry.go:42)\n\n**Issue:** the loop never stops.\n\n**Recommended fix:** cap attempts.",
		"a bold title bullet with details":     "### High\n- **Unbounded retry** (retry.go:42)\n- **Severity:** high\n- **Fix:** cap attempts.",
		"a bold fix paragraph":                 "### High\n\n**Unbounded retry** (retry.go:42)\nThe loop never stops on 503.\n\n**Fix:** cap attempts at 5.\n\n### Low\nNone.",
	} {
		t.Run("comments covering "+name+" are posted as structured findings", func(t *testing.T) {
			t.Parallel()
			report, called, _ := postedTrailReport(t, reviewers, prose+"\n"+oneHighComment)
			if !called || len(report.Comments) != 1 || report.Prose != "" {
				t.Fatalf("called=%v report=%+v, want the one structured comment and no prose", called, report)
			}
		})
	}

	t.Run("null comments is not clean", func(t *testing.T) {
		t.Parallel()
		report, called, _ := postedTrailReport(t, reviewers, "approve — fine\n"+`{"summary":"","comments":null}`)
		requirePostedProse(t, report, called, "approve — fine")
